# Contributors and provenance

This standalone repository records an extraction boundary for work developed in
[NousResearch/hermes-agent PR #65982](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/65982).
The names below are public Git author or attribution identifiers verified in the
inspected source history and commit bodies. They are not a maintainer list, and
they do not imply that each person authored every file in this repository.

## Verified source-history contributors

- `fcavalcantirj` — initial Claude Agent SDK provider landing, runtime and
  documentation follow-ups, and the PR tip.
- `CryptoKylan` — Claude SDK runtime, transport, safety, context, and test
  changes in the PR history.
- `PyroFilmsFX` — SDK startup, stream, and gateway integration follow-ups.
- `Romain` — source Git author for the hybrid MCP bridge work; merge metadata
  also identifies this contributor as `romain-bury`.

## Explicit bridge attribution

The source body of commit
[`8380da12`](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/commit/8380da12df9650674cf23ec04dcbc7bc6813570d)
credits the shared `hermes_tool_exposure.py` layer and in-process bridge design
to Akshay CM (`akshaynexus/hermes-agent`), based on
[PR #56413](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/56413). This is a
specific bridge-design attribution, not an authorship claim for all plugin
code.

The source history also contains generic author display names such as
`Hermes Agent`; those are not listed as human contributors. Codex, the
extractor, and this documentation lane are not authors of the upstream work.

This file intentionally contains no contributor email addresses. Source commit
trailers and any tool-assisted co-author metadata remain subject to the
history-preserving extraction policy; this document is a sanitized provenance
summary, not a replacement for the source graph.
